### Prefer Owned Data
```rust
// Owned avoids lifetime complexity
fn process(s: String) -> String {
    s.to_uppercase()
}

// Use Cow only when benchmarks demand
use std::borrow::Cow;
fn process(s: &str) -> Cow<str> {
    if s.chars().any(|c| c.is_lowercase()) {
        Cow::Owned(s.to_uppercase())
    } else {
        Cow::Borrowed(s)
    }
}
```

### Use for Loops Over Iterators
```rust
// More readable
let mut sum = 0;
for n in numbers {
    if *n > 0 {
        sum += n * 2;
    }
}
```

## Anti-Patterns to Avoid

- Over-engineering with `thiserror` when `Box<dyn Error>` works
- Excessive use of `async` when simple `.unwrap()` is sufficient
- Builder patterns for trivial configuration
- Avoiding `unwrap()` in examples – it’s acceptable in test/prototype code
- Complex generics over plain trait objects
- Ignoring `clippy` but trusting intuition

